e complemented with the Konstanz method of dilemma discussion. Intl J Ethics Education. 2016;1(1):81–89. doi: 10.1007/s40889-016-0009-8. [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] Seshan, V., G. A. Matua, D. Raghavan, J. Arulappan, I. Al Hashmi, E. J. Roach, … E. J. Prince. 2021. Case study analysis as an effective teaching strategy: Perceptions of undergraduate nursing students from a middle Eastern Country. SAGE Open Nursing , 7. 10.1177/23779608211059265 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] Sverdlik N, Rechter E. Religious and secular roads to justify wrongdoing: How values interact with culture in explaining moral disengagement attitudes. J Res Pers. 2020;87:103981. doi: 10.1016/j.jrp.2020.103981. [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] Tao, Y., Y. Cai, C. Rana, and Y. Zhong. 2020. The impact of the extraversion-introversion personality traits and emotions in a moral decision-making task. Personality and Individual Differences, 158 (January). 10.1016/j.paid.2020.109840. Tillman, C.J., K. Gonzalez, M.V. Whitman, W.S. Crawford, and A.C. Hood. 2018. A multi-functional view of moral disengagement: Exploring the effects of learning the consequences. Frontiers in Psychology, 8 (JAN). 10.3389/FPSYG.2017.02286. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] Yap-Figueras JG. Case study discussion for students’ comprehension of the four bioethics principles. WVSU Res J. 2013;2(2):43–53. [ Google Scholar ] Yap-Figueras JG. Predictive models of biology students’ convictions towards bioethical issues. Intl J Ethics Education. 2019;4(2):147–165. doi: 10.1007/s40889-019-00072-0. [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] Yilmaz, O., H. G. Bahçekapili, B. Sevi. 2019. Theory of moral development. In Encyclopedia of evolutionary psychological science , ed. ed. Todd K. Shackelford, Viviana A. Weekes-Shackelford. 1-5. Springer. 10.1007/978-3-319-16999-6_171-1 Associated Data This section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in this article. Supplementary Materials ESM 1 (1