gle Scholar ] 13. Robinson Whitney R. (@WhitneyEpi), et al. Ok, non-U.S. #epitwitter, I need info for a commentary I’m writing. How is population-based gynecologic research (e.g., #endo, #fibroids, #PCOS) funded in your country? 1/n.2019. https://twitter.com/WhitneyEpi/status/1180214195943563267?s=20 (accessed 16 Feb 2020). 14. Gynecologic Health and Disease Research at NICHD. https://www.nichd.nih.gov/sites/default/files/2018-06/GHDB_ScientificVision_2018.pdf (accessed 25 Oct 2019). 15. Women’s Reproductive Health Research (WRHR) Career Development Program. https://www.nichd.nih.gov/.https://www.nichd.nih.gov/research/supported/wrhr (accessed 22 Jul 2020). 16. Ghant MS, Sengoba KS, Vogelzang R, et al. An Altered Perception of Normal: Understanding Causes for Treatment Delay in Women with Symptomatic Uterine Fibroids. J Womens Health 2016;25:846–52. doi: 10.1089/jwh.2015.5531 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 17. Chibber S, Mendoza G, Cohen L, et al. Racial and ethnic differences in uterine fibroid prevalence in a diverse cohort of young asymptomatic women (18–30 yo). Fertil Steril 2016;106:e97. doi: 10.1016/j.fertnstert.2016.07.281 [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 18. Sengoba KS, Ghant MS, Okeigwe I, et al. Racial/Ethnic Differences in Women’s Experiences with Symptomatic Uterine Fibroids: a Qualitative Assessment. J Racial Ethn Health Disparities 2017;4:178–83. doi: 10.1007/s40615-016-0216-1 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 19. Nnoaham KE, Hummelshoj L, Webster P, et al. Impact of endometriosis on quality of life and work productivity: a multicenter study across ten countries. Fertil Steril 2011. ;96:366–373.e8. doi: 10.1016/j.fertnstert.2011.05.090 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 20. Brandão P, Portela-Carvalho A, Oliveira C. Non-Painful Out of Pill Membranous Dysmenorrhoea. Obstet Gynaecol Cases - Rev 2018;5. doi: 10.23937/2377-9004/1410137 [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 21. Leung AKC, Pacaud D.